WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.822
My next guest went from the private sector

2
00:00:02.822 --> 00:00:04.731
as the CEO of Coca-Cola in Mexico,

3
00:00:04.731 --> 00:00:07.480
to the public sector as the President of Mexico,

4
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.824
sounds familiar actually,

5
00:00:08.824 --> 00:00:13.154
please welcome former president, Vicente Fox.

6
00:00:13.154 --> 00:00:17.071
(audience applauds and cheers)

7
00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:30.482
You brought me a gift, thank you so much.

8
00:00:30.482 --> 00:00:31.802
These are boots.

9
00:00:31.802 --> 00:00:32.903
There's writing on it.

10
00:00:32.903 --> 00:00:34.570
No wall.

11
00:00:36.586 --> 00:00:37.419
No wall.

12
00:00:39.128 --> 00:00:40.989
Thank you, thank you.

13
00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:42.896
You’ve made it quite certain I will not be going back

14
00:00:42.896 --> 00:00:44.646
to the United States.

15
00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:46.664
Made in Mexico,

16
00:00:46.664 --> 00:00:48.368
by the best--
Yeah, made in Mexico.

17
00:00:48.368 --> 00:00:50.191
Yeah I would think so.

18
00:00:50.191 --> 00:00:51.558
Have a seat, please, sir.

19
00:00:51.558 --> 00:00:52.391
Of the world.

20
00:00:52.391 --> 00:00:53.224
Thank you so much.

21
00:00:53.224 --> 00:00:56.826
These are beautiful, and I will wear these often.

22
00:00:56.826 --> 00:00:59.576
Yes, we have so much to talk about.

23
00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:03.006
First of all, I get the sense that you have an opinion

24
00:01:03.006 --> 00:01:04.256
about the wall.

25
00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.498
Not just from the boots,

26
00:01:06.498 --> 00:01:09.007
but from some of your very colorful Tweets

27
00:01:09.007 --> 00:01:10.976
that you've sent out.

28
00:01:10.976 --> 00:01:13.954
Your use of language crosses all barriers.

29
00:01:13.954 --> 00:01:15.704
It's great.

30
00:01:15.704 --> 00:01:16.642
Now, what's interesting,

31
00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:17.589
let's talk about the history,

32
00:01:17.589 --> 00:01:19.269
because you make an interesting point.

33
00:01:19.269 --> 00:01:20.613
One of your opinions is,

34
00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:23.718
throughout history, walls have not worked.

35
00:01:23.718 --> 00:01:25.928
That is absolutely real.

36
00:01:25.928 --> 00:01:29.983
We all remember when President Reagan came to Berlin,

37
00:01:29.983 --> 00:01:34.150
he said, "Mr. Gorbachev, tear down off that wall."

38
00:01:35.948 --> 00:01:36.968
No, no.

39
00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:37.916
I was there.

40
00:01:37.916 --> 00:01:40.024
He didn't say that.

41
00:01:40.024 --> 00:01:41.731
(audience laughs)

42
00:01:41.731 --> 00:01:43.448
Your history is good President Fox,

43
00:01:43.448 --> 00:01:45.390
but it's not perfect.

44
00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.804
But yes, the Berlin Wall famously failed.

45
00:01:47.804 --> 00:01:48.764
It doesn't work.

46
00:01:48.764 --> 00:01:51.155
Freedom, terror off.

47
00:01:51.155 --> 00:01:53.187
Walls don't work.

48
00:01:53.187 --> 00:01:55.475
And especially when we,

49
00:01:55.475 --> 00:01:59.256
the people of United States, and Mexico,

50
00:01:59.256 --> 00:02:02.272
we are neighbors, we're friends,

51
00:02:02.272 --> 00:02:04.166
we're partners,

52
00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:07.395
and most so, we're roommates.

53
00:02:07.395 --> 00:02:09.878
We are so much together,

54
00:02:09.878 --> 00:02:12.601
so many good friendship.

55
00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:16.046
So many Mexicans doing a great work,

56
00:02:16.046 --> 00:02:18.529
loyal to the United States.

57
00:02:18.529 --> 00:02:20.687
Making that economy competitive.

58
00:02:20.687 --> 00:02:23.615
And now they want to kick them in the ass,

59
00:02:23.615 --> 00:02:25.800
and throw them out.

60
00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.999
That's going to be a big, big loss for United States.

61
00:02:29.999 --> 00:02:33.916
(audience cheers and applauds)

62
00:02:38.636 --> 00:02:41.514
I live in Los Angeles, and I've said this before,

63
00:02:41.514 --> 00:02:45.919
but you cannot walk three feet in Los Angeles

64
00:02:45.919 --> 00:02:48.655
and not be made aware of

65
00:02:48.655 --> 00:02:50.803
the incredible cultural contributions,

66
00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.803
food, art, architecture,

67
00:02:53.683 --> 00:02:56.621
that have been made by Mexicans.

68
00:02:56.621 --> 00:02:58.290
And so it's very silly.

69
00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.524
We are already together.

70
00:02:59.524 --> 00:03:00.438
We are already together,

71
00:03:00.438 --> 00:03:01.916
and that is not going to change.

72
00:03:01.916 --> 00:03:02.749
Yes, sir.

73
00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.915
And I was working in a ranch in Mexico,

74
00:03:04.915 --> 00:03:08.082
and grew with campesinos at the ranch.

75
00:03:09.702 --> 00:03:12.966
And I remember when there were tears in the eyes,

76
00:03:12.966 --> 00:03:16.028
they will come and say, "Good bye.”

77
00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:17.372
"We're moving North.”

78
00:03:17.372 --> 00:03:19.553
"We're looking for opportunities.”

79
00:03:19.553 --> 00:03:23.503
"We want to make some money to have a better life

80
00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.734
for ourselves and for our family."

81
00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:28.067
Good, loyal, loving, people.

82
00:03:29.059 --> 00:03:30.678
They worked for the Bush family,

83
00:03:30.678 --> 00:03:33.030
they worked for the Trump family.

84
00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.987
They might not have documents,

85
00:03:34.987 --> 00:03:36.716
but they know how to work.

86
00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.275
They are decent.

87
00:03:38.275 --> 00:03:39.869
They're honest.

88
00:03:39.869 --> 00:03:43.158
And they contribute to the greatness of that nation.

89
00:03:43.158 --> 00:03:44.877
So America is great,

90
00:03:44.877 --> 00:03:47.481
(audience applauds and cheers)

91
00:03:47.481 --> 00:03:51.648
and it will be greater because of our people right there.

92
00:03:53.107 --> 00:03:55.782
There's been talk about why is Trump angry about Mexico,

93
00:03:55.782 --> 00:03:56.934
there's a rumor that I've heard

94
00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.134
that he had properties in Mexico,

95
00:03:58.134 --> 00:04:00.158
and maybe there was some difficulties.

96
00:04:00.158 --> 00:04:02.784
He tried to build one of his towers

97
00:04:02.784 --> 00:04:04.703
in the Gulf of the Cortez,

98
00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:06.265
which is in Baja.

99
00:04:06.265 --> 00:04:08.710
It's a sanctuary of nature,

100
00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:09.791
beautiful,

101
00:04:09.791 --> 00:04:11.965
and he wanted to build one of his towers.

102
00:04:11.965 --> 00:04:14.507
Of course, he was not allowed to.

103
00:04:14.507 --> 00:04:15.997
It was prohibited.

104
00:04:15.997 --> 00:04:17.280
And he got mad with Mexicans.

105
00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.509
But maybe it has to do also with color.

106
00:04:20.509 --> 00:04:22.406
You're quite white.

107
00:04:22.406 --> 00:04:23.510
You're blonde.

108
00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:24.565
What are you talking about?

109
00:04:24.565 --> 00:04:25.728
I though I,

110
00:04:25.728 --> 00:04:26.675
wait a minute,

111
00:04:26.675 --> 00:04:30.717
I think I blend in quite nicely in this country.

112
00:04:30.717 --> 00:04:32.099
I was in a telenovela, man.

113
00:04:32.099 --> 00:04:32.932
Back off.

114
00:04:33.986 --> 00:04:35.653
I sell cheese, dude.

115
00:04:37.023 --> 00:04:41.287
But he doesn't seem to like the brown color.

116
00:04:41.287 --> 00:04:42.537
And it's awful.

117
00:04:44.088 --> 00:04:47.957
We Mexicans are "chiquitos pero picosos".

118
00:04:47.957 --> 00:04:51.339
(audience applauds)

119
00:04:51.339 --> 00:04:53.333
We might be short,

120
00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:56.117
but we're hot like a jalapeno.

121
00:04:56.117 --> 00:05:00.401
So don't mess around with us, Senior Trump.

122
00:05:00.401 --> 00:05:04.517
Because if you look for it, you're going to find it.

123
00:05:04.517 --> 00:05:07.301
(audience cheers and applauds)

124
00:05:07.301 --> 00:05:09.989
Today, Rex Tillerson, the Secretary of State,

125
00:05:09.989 --> 00:05:11.764
is visiting Mexico.

126
00:05:11.764 --> 00:05:13.995
Do you think he's going to be proposing peace?

127
00:05:13.995 --> 00:05:16.153
Is he bringing olive branch, in your opinion?

128
00:05:16.153 --> 00:05:19.670
Today, they were playing around a game with the wall,

129
00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.105
and Mexicans paying for the wall.

130
00:05:22.105 --> 00:05:25.875
And they come with that instruction from Trump,

131
00:05:25.875 --> 00:05:29.366
to try to convince us to pay for the wall.

132
00:05:29.366 --> 00:05:33.533
Please, Mr. Trump, we're not paying for that wall.

133
00:05:34.781 --> 00:05:36.580
That is very clear.

134
00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.460
(audience cheers)

135
00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.908
Can I just say one thing?

136
00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:46.075
President Fox, I appreciate that you talking to Trump,

137
00:05:47.064 --> 00:05:50.989
but I think he switched channels very early in this program.

138
00:05:50.989 --> 00:05:53.572
(Conan laughs)

139
00:05:54.973 --> 00:05:57.207
We very much wanted you to come on the show,

140
00:05:57.207 --> 00:05:59.284
and give us your perspective.

141
00:05:59.284 --> 00:06:00.881
Our mission here has been

142
00:06:00.881 --> 00:06:03.554
to bring positivity and optimism,

143
00:06:03.554 --> 00:06:05.476
and humanize the situation.

144
00:06:05.476 --> 00:06:09.255
But I was very honored you took the time to fly down here--

145
00:06:09.255 --> 00:06:11.347
May I give a little bit of advice to the guy?

146
00:06:11.347 --> 00:06:13.352
Yeah, sure.

147
00:06:13.352 --> 00:06:15.440
If he wants to negotiate,

148
00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:18.968
we have to go for the whole enchilada.

149
00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:20.322
Not just one piece.

150
00:06:20.322 --> 00:06:24.147
Not just trading, not just security.

151
00:06:24.147 --> 00:06:28.314
He has to learn that we are his best friends and partners.

152
00:06:31.928 --> 00:06:33.095
You like some?

153
00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:36.910
You know what I love about ...

154
00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:40.319
(audience cheers and applauds)

155
00:06:40.319 --> 00:06:42.802
You know what I really love about you, President Fox,

156
00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.635
is that you use great visual aids,

157
00:06:47.014 --> 00:06:48.826
to demonstrate.

158
00:06:48.826 --> 00:06:52.743
(audience cheers and applauds)

159
00:06:54.345 --> 00:06:56.275
President Vicente Fox everybody.

160
00:06:56.275 --> 00:06:58.942
Much more Mexico when we return.

